## Plan: Add spinner indicator for actively-worked items

### 1. TUI: `pipeline/tui.py` — `FeatureItem` class

**1a. Add `is_active` parameter to `__init__`**
- Add `is_active: bool = False` param after `is_selected`
- Store `self.is_active = is_active`
- Add class constants: `_spinner_frames = "⣾⣽⣻⢿⡿⣟⣯⣷"` and `self._frame = 0`
- Extract a `_render_label()` helper that returns the markup string:
  - If active: return `f" {spinner_char}  {display_name}"` with cyan Rich markup
  - Otherwise: return existing `f"    {display_name}{indicator}"` format
- Pass `self._render_label()` to `super().__init__()` instead of the inline string
- Add `--active` to CSS classes when `is_active` is True

**1b. Add `on_mount` handler**
- If `self.is_active`, call `self.set_interval(0.1, self._advance_spinner)`

**1c. Add `_advance_spinner` method**
- Increment `self._frame = (self._frame + 1) % len(self._spinner_frames)`
- Call `self.update(self._render_label())`

**1d. Update `_refresh_kanban_widgets`**
- Before the feature loop, compute `active_slugs: set[str]`:
  - If `self._plan_running` and `self._plan_agent_status.feature_slug`: add it
  - If `self._implement_running` and `self._implement_agent_status.feature_slug`: add it
- Pass `is_active=f.slug in active_slugs` to each `FeatureItem(...)` constructor
- No extra cleanup needed: `_on_plan_done` and `_on_implement_done` both call `_refresh_board` → `_refresh_kanban_widgets`, which rebuilds all widgets with `is_active=False`

**1e. Add CSS rule**
- Add `.feature-item.--active { color: cyan; }` in the app's CSS

### 2. Server client: `pipeline/server_client.py`

- In `push_state`, add `"slug": f.slug` to each feature summary dict (alongside `"id": f.id`)

### 3. Server: `server/hub.go` — `FeatureSummary` struct

- Add `Slug string \`json:"slug"\`` field to `FeatureSummary` struct
- No other Go changes needed: the slug is populated automatically when the Python client sends the `state_update` message with the `slug` field

### 4. Server API: `server/api.go` — `/api/board` handler

- After collecting `allFeatures`, iterate all clients and collect active feature slugs:
  ```go
  activeSlugs := map[string]bool{}
  for _, c := range clients {
      if c.PlanAgent.Running && c.PlanAgent.Feature != "" {
          activeSlugs[c.PlanAgent.Feature] = true
      }
      if c.ImplAgent.Running && c.ImplAgent.Feature != "" {
          activeSlugs[c.ImplAgent.Feature] = true
      }
  }
  ```
- Add `"ActiveSlugs": activeSlugs` to the template data map

### 5. Template: `server/templates/index.html`

**5a. Add CSS keyframes and spinner class**
In the `<style>` block:
```css
@keyframes spin { to { transform: rotate(360deg); } }
[data-active="true"] .title::before {
    content: '';
    display: inline-block;
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    border: 2px solid #58a6ff;
    border-top-color: transparent;
    border-radius: 50%;
    animation: spin 0.7s linear infinite;
    vertical-align: middle;
    margin-right: 5px;
}
```

**5b. Add `data-active` attribute to feature cards in `board_fragment`**
```html
data-active="{{if index $.ActiveSlugs .Slug}}true{{end}}"
```
Add this attribute to each `<div class="feature-card">` element.

**5c. Update `cardHash` JS function**
- Include `c.getAttribute('data-active')` in the hash array so cards are replaced when active state changes:
```js
function cardHash(c) {
    return [c.getAttribute('data-id'), c.getAttribute('data-stage'),
            c.getAttribute('data-title'), c.getAttribute('data-description'),
            c.getAttribute('data-history'), c.getAttribute('data-active')].join('|');
}
```

